We sit down to eat.
Priya serves me hot Varan Bhaat and spicy Batata Bhaji.
The food smells very nice.
I take the first bite.
I tell Priya, "Priya, this food is very tasty!"
I think that I will eat this every day.
Priya laughs and thanks me.
Now we are not talking about office work.
We chat about our families.
I tell her about my family in Mexico.
My elder brother's name is Diego and my younger sister's name is Sofia.
I also tell her about our dog named Lola.
Priya tells me her childhood memories.
She says that her entire childhood was spent right in Mumbai.
"After dinner, let's look at my old photos," Priya says.
I happily agree.
I think that now we will have a very nice friendship.
While chatting, we don't even realize when our meal ends.
